::Q1::Which data warehouse is Amazon Web Services' offering? 
{
~Google BigQuery
~Snowflake
~Google Cloud SQL
=Amazon Redshift
}

::Q2::Which platform is notable for its serverless design? 
{
=Google BigQuery
~Amazon Redshift
~Amazon EC2
~Snowflake
}

::Q3::Why might an AWS-heavy organization choose Redshift? 
{
~It is designed only for Google Cloud
~It automatically converts every workload into a data lake
~It is the only warehouse that can run outside the cloud
=It integrates closely with the organization's existing AWS ecosystem
}

::Q4::What does cloud-agnostic mean in the context of a warehouse platform such as Snowflake? 
{
~The platform requires an organization to own physical servers
~The platform can run only on AWS
~The platform cannot use cloud infrastructure
=The platform can run across multiple major cloud providers rather than being tied to one
}

::Q5::Why can limiting columns and rows in a query affect cost on scan-based platforms? 
{
=Scanning less data can reduce the amount of data processed by the query
~The number of selected columns has no possible relationship to scanned data
~Filtering rows prevents a query from executing
~Selecting fewer columns always increases the amount of data scanned
}